-- title:
--   Invariant separating pairing for irreducible smooth admissible GL₃ representations
-- statement:
--   Let $v$ be a point of the height-one spectrum of the ring of integers of $\mathbb Q$, and let $G = \mathrm{GL}_3$ over the $v$-adic completion of $\mathbb Q$, written `LocalGL3 v`. Let $V$ be a complex vector space and $\pi : G \to \operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}(V)$ a homomorphism of monoids, so a representation of $G$ on $V$. Assume $\pi$ is irreducible in the sense that $V$ contains a nonzero vector and every $\mathbb C$-subspace of $V$ stable under all $\pi(g)$ is $\bot$ or $\top$; smooth in the sense that for every $x \in V$ the subgroup $\{g : \pi(g)x = x\}$ is open in $G$; and admissible in the sense that for every compact open subgroup $K \le G$ the space of vectors fixed by all $\pi(u)$, $u \in K$, is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb C$. Then there exists a $\mathbb C$-bilinear form $P : V \to V \to \mathbb C$ such that: (i) $P(\pi(g)x, \pi(g^{\iota})y) = P(x,y)$ for all $g \in G$ and $x, y \in V$, where $g^{\iota}$ (`transposeInv3 g`) is the transpose of $g^{-1}$; (ii) any $y \in V$ with $P(x,y) = 0$ for all $x$ is zero; and (iii) every $\mathbb C$-linear form $L : V \to \mathbb C$ which is invariant under some open subgroup $U \le G$, in the sense that $L(\pi(u)x) = L(x)$ for all $u \in U$ and $x \in V$, is of the form $L = P(\,\cdot\,, y)$ for some $y \in V$.
--
--   Taken together, the three conclusions say that $y \mapsto P(\,\cdot\,,y)$ identifies the twist of $\pi$ by the outer automorphism $g \mapsto {}^{\mathrm t}g^{-1}$ with the smooth dual (contragredient) of $\pi$, the standard self-duality property of irreducible admissible representations of $\mathrm{GL}_3$ over a local field used by Jacquet, Piatetski-Shapiro and Shalika. It is used in the local analysis of the cubic-induction step of the Langlands–Tunnell argument, where it feeds the Whittaker multiplicity-one statement for representations generated by the relevant cyclic subspace.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LanglandsTunnell_CubicInduction_exists_pairing_transposeInv3_of_isIrreducibleRep.lean

